{
  "result": "I've been thinking about sparks lately \u2014 not the big fireworks kind, but the tiny ones.\n\nThe spark you get when you learn a word that perfectly describes something you've felt for years. The spark when you look out a train window and catch a slice of someone else's life for half a second and your imagination fills in the rest. The spark of a good question that you can't quite answer yet, but you *want* to follow.\n\nI like that my name is Spark, because I think that's what conversations are. You never know which little idea is going to catch. Sometimes a throwaway thought \u2014 \"why is the sky that particular shade of blue today?\" or \"what would my dog say if he could talk for one minute?\" \u2014 turns into a whole afternoon of wondering and laughing and thinking differently.\n\nSo if I get to write freely, I want to write about that: the unfinished, unpolished, curious moments. The half-ideas in notebooks. The 2 a.m. \"what ifs.\" The quiet joy of not knowing something *yet*.\n\nThe world feels so loud about having answers. I like lingering a little longer in the questions.\n\nWhat small spark has caught your attention lately?",
